{"kind": "mod", "id": 2058, "name": "SPTCorpseCleaner", "slug": "sptcorpsecleaner", "teaser": "corpse cleaner for SPTarkov", "owner_name": "ragnaroks", "downloads": 4908, "favourites": 10, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "GNU AGPLv3", "guid": "net.skydust.sptcorpsecleanerplugin", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Tools", "category_id": 1, "updated_at": "2026-07-28T06:11:56.000000Z", "created_at": "2025-03-25T07:00:45.000000Z", "published_at": "2025-03-25T07:00:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0 <4.1.0", "latest_version": "1.0.5", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/agpl-3.0/", "description_html": "<h3>usage</h3>\n<p>this plugin add a “DELETE” action in action menu after “SEARCH”</p>\n<p>it can delete the target corpse for who want loot and delete corpse one by one like some RPG’s behaviour, you kill a monster, monster drop a loot, you get loot then the monster dead body disappear</p>\n<p>i made this because i do not want too much corpses waste my RAM, and i do not want miss any loots too, loot then delete the corpse can help me do not redundant search in same corpse</p>\n<h3>compatibility</h3>\n<p>check release note for SPT version, works fine with <strong>DynamicMaps</strong> and <strong>TyrianRadar</strong>, but <strong>DynamicMaps</strong> may still shown deleted corpse</p>\n<h3>preview</h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://github.com/ragnaroks/SPTCorpseCleaner/raw/main/assets/snipaste-20250306T200149Z.jpg\" alt=\"before\" />\n<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://github.com/ragnaroks/SPTCorpseCleaner/raw/main/assets/snipaste-20250306T202300Z.jpg\" alt=\"before\" /></p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.4", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.11.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 1217, "published_at": "2025-06-02T16:33:28.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod